-- title:
--   §3, p. 8 — a family of events with dependence at most b
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,\mu)$ be a probability space and $A_1,\dots,A_m\in\mathcal F$ events. Following p. 8 of Leighton, Maggs and Rao, the family has **dependence at most $b$** if every event is mutually independent of some set of $m-b-1$ other events: for every $i$ there is a set $S\subseteq\{1,\dots,m\}\setminus\{i\}$ with $|S|\ge m-b-1$ such that $A_i$ is independent of the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $\{A_j : j\in S\}$,
--   $$
--   \mu(A_i\cap B)=\mu(A_i)\,\mu(B)\qquad\text{for all } B\in\sigma(A_j : j\in S).
--   $$
--   This is mutual independence of $A_i$ from the whole subfamily, not pairwise independence. It is the dependence notion of the Lovász Local Lemma as the paper uses it.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "A set of $m-b-1$ others" is written as $|S|+b+1\ge m$, which avoids truncated subtraction when $b\ge m$; since independence passes to subfamilies, it is the same as $|S|=m-b-1$ whenever $b<m$. Independence is Mathlib's `ProbabilityTheory.Indep` of the generated $\sigma$-algebras.
-- source:
--   Leighton, Maggs & Rao, Packet routing and job-shop scheduling in O(congestion + dilation) steps, authors' manuscript (preprint of Combinatorica 14 (1994), DOI 10.1007/BF01215349), p. 8, definition of dependence before Lemma 3.1

import Mathlib

namespace PacketRouting.CongDil

open MeasureTheory

/-- **Dependence at most `b`** (Leighton–Maggs–Rao, p. 8): "A set of events `A₁, …, A_m` in a
probability space has dependence at most `b` if every event is mutually independent of some set
of `m − b − 1` other bad events." For every `i` there is a set `S` of indices, not containing
`i`, of size at least `m − b − 1` (written `m ≤ |S| + b + 1` to avoid truncated subtraction),
such that `A_i` is independent of the σ-algebra generated by the events `A_j`, `j ∈ S` (mutual
independence of `A_i` from the family `(A_j)_{j ∈ S}`, not pairwise independence). Since
independence passes to subfamilies, "at least `m − b − 1`" is the same as "exactly `m − b − 1`"
whenever `b < m`. -/
def HasDependenceAtMost {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) {m : ℕ}
    (A : Fin m → Set Ω) (b : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ i : Fin m, ∃ S : Finset (Fin m), i ∉ S ∧ m ≤ S.card + b + 1 ∧
    ProbabilityTheory.Indep (MeasurableSpace.generateFrom {A i})
      (MeasurableSpace.generateFrom (A '' (S : Set (Fin m)))) μ

end PacketRouting.CongDil


